  "definition": "Python is a high-level, dynamically typed, interpreted programming language with a design philosophy emphasising code readability and the minimisation of syntactic ceremony. Its extensive standard library and the PyPI ecosystem of third-party packages\u2014including NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, PyTorch, TensorFlow, and Scikit-learn\u2014make it the dominant language for machine learning research, data science, and scientific computing. Python's combination of interactive development via Jupyter notebooks, a permissive licence, and first-class support in cloud ML platforms has made it the lingua franca of artificial intelligence development.",
